From 3e88d130ba173ea569bd6ef15463d7d619942a4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allixender <alexander.kmoch@ut.ee>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:23:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] DgAuthalic: double tolerance for the inverse on quad long
 double

authalicToGeodeticLatitude() iterates until the residual is below
8 * LDBL_EPSILON. On aarch64 linux long double is IEEE quad (epsilon
1.9e-34), but musl's log1pl() for 113-bit long double is log1p() in
double precision ("TODO: broken implementation to make things compile"),
and atanhl() goes through log1pl(). q() and polarAreaDeficit() therefore
carry ~1e-16 relative noise, neither stopping rule can be met within the
64 iterations and DGGRID stops with

  FATAL ERROR: DgAuthalic::authalicToGeodeticLatitude: inverse did not converge

(examples icosaISEAL and wholeEarthIGEO7v2, static musl build on
ubuntu-24.04-arm). Use 8 * DBL_EPSILON when long double has more than 64
mantissa bits. double and x87 long double builds are unchanged.

This is the workaround for the musl builds. For upstream a stall
criterion (accept the iterate once the bracket stops shrinking) would
keep the full precision on a libm with real quad log1pl (glibc).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/lib/dglib/lib/DgAuthalicConverter.cpp | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/lib/dglib/lib/DgAuthalicConverter.cpp b/src/lib/dglib/lib/DgAuthalicConverter.cpp
index 103e068..1806143 100644
--- a/src/lib/dglib/lib/DgAuthalicConverter.cpp
+++ b/src/lib/dglib/lib/DgAuthalicConverter.cpp
@@ -135,8 +135,14 @@ long double DgAuthalic::authalicToGeodeticLatitude(long double beta)
    long double low = 0.0L;
    long double high = halfPi;
    long double t = usePolarComplement ? halfPi - absBeta : absBeta;
-   const long double tolerance =
-      8.0L * std::numeric_limits<long double>::epsilon();
+   // A long double wider than x87 extended (IEEE quad, aarch64 linux) is not
+   // matched by every libm: musl evaluates log1pl(), and atanhl() through it,
+   // in double precision there. q() then cannot resolve 8 * LDBL_EPSILON and
+   // the solve would never converge, so fall back to the double tolerance.
+   const long double tolerance = 8.0L *
+      (std::numeric_limits<long double>::digits > 64
+          ? (long double) std::numeric_limits<double>::epsilon()
+          : std::numeric_limits<long double>::epsilon());
    bool converged = false;
 
    // Both q(phi) and the polar area deficit are monotone. Keep Newton's
